// docs/spec/cheatsheet.charter — Executable Charter 1.0 Language Reference Tour
// Exercises every core Charter 1.0 construct in one self-contained, passing program.
//! explore: 1

// 1. Clauses & SHA-256 Provenance (012)
Clause CS.1 Approved "f430afdf64f733e9b3078b14cd22c4f3bd09dc584589e5c33b014e534aa271b4"
  Text "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds."
  Norm "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds." => release-funds, freeze-shield, adjudicate-kyc
.

// 2. Parameters, Regimes, & Dimensional Types (003, 009, 010, 014)
Param payout-cap : Money(USD, 2) = 50000.
Param hold-window : Duration = 3.

Regime conservative {
  payout-cap = 25000,
  hold-window = 5
}.

// 3. Facts, Evidenced Propositions, & Stratified Default/Exception Rules (003, 004, 007)
Fact steward Identified by Steward1.
Fact beneficiary Identified by Alice, Bob.
Fact arbiter Identified by Arb1.
Fact frozen Identified by beneficiary.
Fact usd-amt Identified by Money(USD, 2).
Fact arbiter-quorum Identified by arbiter.

Evidenced Fact kyc-verified Identified by beneficiary
  Confidential To auditor, arbiter.

Fact eligible-tier Identified by beneficiary
  Default tier-base Holds when True
  Exception tier-frozen Overrides tier-base Rejects when frozen(beneficiary).

// 4. Modules & Instantiation (015)
Module receipt-log(party) {
  Fact paid Identified by party.
}
Use receipt-log(beneficiary) As rl.

// 5. Powers, Findings, Duties, Immunities, & Invariants (005, 006, 007, 013)
Finding adjudicate-kyc Actor arbiter Related to beneficiary
  From CS.1 "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds."
  Resolves kyc-verified(beneficiary)
  Standard preponderance
  Holds when Unresolved(kyc-verified(beneficiary)) || Conflicted(kyc-verified(beneficiary))
  Valid when arbiter-quorum(arbiter).

Power release-funds Actor steward Recipient beneficiary
  From CS.1 "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds."
  Holds when eligible-tier(beneficiary) && kyc-verified(beneficiary) && MulDivRound(10000, 2, 1, ExactOrReject) <= payout-cap
  Valid when eligible-tier(beneficiary) && kyc-verified(beneficiary) && MulDivRound(10000, 2, 1, ExactOrReject) <= payout-cap
  Creates rl-paid(beneficiary) For hold-window.

Immunity freeze-shield Holder beneficiary
  From CS.1 "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds."
  Against release-funds
  Holds when frozen(beneficiary).

Entrenched Invariant paid-implies-verified
  When (Forall beneficiary: Established(kyc-verified(beneficiary)) When rl-paid(beneficiary))
  From CS.1 "A steward may release funds up to the cap to a verified beneficiary unless an immunity holds.".

Property safety-always When WeakUntil(paid-implies-verified(), False).

// 6. Scenarios & Three-Answer Claims (011)
Scenario cheatsheet-tour {
  ?Unresolved(kyc-verified(Alice)).
  ?undetermined release-funds(Steward1, Alice).
  +arbiter-quorum(Arb1).
  adjudicate-kyc(Arb1, Alice).
  ?Established(kyc-verified(Alice)).
  ?valid release-funds(Steward1, Alice).
  release-funds(Steward1, Alice) Note "authorized escrow release".
  ?rl-paid(Alice).
  @ 3.
  ?!rl-paid(Alice).
}
